# TypeScript Standards

## Strictness
- `strict: true` in `tsconfig.json` — never weaken it
- No `any`; use `unknown` + narrowing when the shape is genuinely unknown
- Export types alongside data: demo entries use a shared `DemoSite` interface

```typescript
// content/demos/types.ts
export interface DemoSite {
  slug: string;        // kebab-case, matches /demos/[slug]
  title: string;
  description: string;
  techStack: string[];
  liveUrl?: string;    // external hosted demo
  screenshot: string;  // path under public/demos/<slug>/
}
```

## Style
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/utilities
- Discriminated unions over optional-field guessing
- No non-null assertions (`!`); handle undefined explicitly
- Const-assert registries:

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
export const sites = [{ slug: 'shop-demo' }];

// ✅ GOOD
export const sites = [
  { slug: 'shop-demo', title: 'Shop Demo', /* ... */ },
] satisfies DemoSite[];
```

## Imports
- `@/` alias for cross-directory imports; relative only within the same folder
- Type-only imports: `import type { DemoSite } from '@/content/demos/types'`
